{"type":"standard","title":"Blake Moore","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Blake Moore</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q101196971","titles":{"canonical":"Blake_Moore","normalized":"Blake Moore","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Blake Moore</span></span>"},"pageid":64472323,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Rep._Blake_Moore_official_photo%2C_2022.jpg/330px-Rep._Blake_Moore_official_photo%2C_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":412},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a4/Rep._Blake_Moore_official_photo%2C_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2143,"height":2678},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1376284732","tid":"4891bbf0-b712-11f1-82ee-310ecade80d4","timestamp":"2026-09-23T05:47:38Z","description":"American politician (born 1980)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blake_Moore","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blake_Moore?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blake_Moore?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Blake_Moore"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blake_Moore","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Blake_Moore","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blake_Moore?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Blake_Moore"}},"extract":"Blake David Moore is an American politician and former diplomat from the state of Utah. He is the U.S. representative for Utah's 1st congressional district, serving since January 2021. Since November 8, 2023, he has been the vice chair of the House Republican Conference.","extract_html":"<p><b>Blake David Moore</b> is an American politician and former diplomat from the state of Utah. He is the U.S. representative for Utah's 1st congressional district, serving since January 2021. Since November 8, 2023, he has been the vice chair of the House Republican Conference.</p>"}